Notebook[{Cell["Finite bubble-difference basis for the nested triangle", 
   "Title"], Cell["This notebook implements the finite convention selected \
for Section 2. It proves the cancellation of the common bubble divergence, \
uses Ly=log(D10/D6) and Lx=log(D10/D5), constructs the finite nested outer \
basis required by the partial_a orbit, and exposes the forced \
lower-block-triangular connection. Exact derived entries and still-unreduced \
outer-IBP slots are deliberately kept distinct.", "Text"], 
  Cell["1. Load the implementation", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "\"Global`*\"", "]"}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"notebookDirectory", "=", RowBox[{"Quiet", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Check", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", 
                "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"DirectoryName", "[", "$InputFileName", 
                "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"Get", "[", RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"notebookDirectory", ",", 
              "\"CosmologicalBaikovFiniteNested.wl\""}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
      ";"}]], "Input"], Cell["2. Why equation (24) has no extra half-power", 
   "Section"], Cell["Equation (24) is correct as printed. The evaluated \
four-dimensional triangle T111 already contains its leading-singularity \
factor Lambda^(-1/2). Indeed its homogeneous derivative is partial_a \
T111=(Q3^2/(2 Lambda)) T111+..., exactly the derivative of Lambda^(-1/2). The \
rational and logarithmic sectors therefore have outer exponent zero, while \
only the triangle sector has effective exponent 1/2.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"exponentAudit", "=", 
        RowBox[{"OuterExponentAudit", "[", "]"}]}], ";", "exponentAudit"}]], 
   "Input"], Cell["3. Finite bubble differences", "Section"], 
  Cell["Let x=D5=Q2^2, y=D6=Q3^2, z=D4=Q2.Q3 and s=D10=(Q2-Q3)^2. The \
coefficients of {T011,T101,T110} in the last line of equation (31) sum to \
zero. Hence the common UV pole and the additive bubble-scheme constant cancel \
before the p2,p3 integration.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"poleCancellation", "=", 
        RowBox[{"BubblePoleCancellationA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", RowBox[{"poleCancellation", ",", "0", 
          ",", RowBox[{"TestID", "\[Rule]", 
            "\"common-bubble-pole-and-constant-cancel\""}]}], "]"}]}]], 
   "Input"], Cell["The two finite weights are Ly=T101-T011=log(D10/D6) and \
Lx=T110-T011=log(D10/D5). The exact finite form of the new term in equation \
(31) is shown below.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"finiteEquation31Source", "=", 
        RowBox[{"FiniteEquation31SourceA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      "finiteEquation31Source"}]], "Input"], 
  Cell["4. Exact flat-weight connection", "Section"], 
  Cell["In the order {1,Ly,Lx,T111}, partial_a acts as partial_x at fixed \
p2,p3,b,c. This matrix is exact and lower triangular. It is the local input \
for the lifted outer IBP system.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"directFlatConnectionA", "=", 
        RowBox[{"DirectFlatWeightConnectionA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      TagBox["directFlatConnectionA", Function[BoxForm`e$, 
        MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]}]], "Input"], 
  Cell["5. Why shifted outer denominators are required", "Section"], 
  Cell["Differentiating Ly and Lx generates 1/D10 and 1/D5. These \
denominators are parallel to D1 and D2, respectively. Products are resolved \
by partial fractions, but both line choices must be retained as distinct mass \
families unless their mass differences vanish.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"parallelDenominatorIdentities", "=", 
        RowBox[{"ParallelDenominatorIdentitiesA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      "parallelDenominatorIdentities"}]], "Input"], 
  Cell["6. Finite extended basis for the partial_a orbit", "Section"], 
  Cell["The rational part is the union of the four ordinary-vacuum families \
R_i P_j Q_0, with R_0=D1, R_1=D10, P_0=D2, P_1=D5 and Q_0=D3. Empty and \
one-line sectors are scaleless in dimensional regularization. There are eight \
factorized two-line masters and four sunrise masters, hence twelve rational \
masters. The diagonal logarithmic problem is also an ordinary vacuum family, \
so each finite logarithm needs only {RP,RQ,PQ,RPQ}. The triangle retains the \
eleven square-root-twisted masters derived previously. The finite basis \
therefore has 12+4+4+11=31 components.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"rationalBasis", "=", 
        RowBox[{"RationalOuterBasisA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"finiteNestedBasis", "=", RowBox[{"FiniteNestedBasisA", "[", 
          "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"blockDimensions", "=", 
        RowBox[{"FiniteNestedBlockDimensionsA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"rational count\"", "\[Rule]", 
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "rationalBasis", "]"}]}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"\"total count\"", "\[Rule]", RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
              "finiteNestedBasis", "]"}]}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"\"block dimensions\"", "\[Rule]", "blockDimensions"}], 
          ",", RowBox[{"\"duplicate free\"", "\[Rule]", 
            RowBox[{"DuplicateFreeQ", "[", "finiteNestedBasis", "]"}]}]}], 
        "}"}]}]], "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Dataset", "[", RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
        RowBox[{RowBox[{"Range", "[", RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
              "finiteNestedBasis", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "finiteNestedBasis"}], 
        "]"}], "]"}]], "Input"], 
  Cell["7. Connection and triangular filtration", "Section"], 
  Cell["In the order {rational,Ly,Lx,triangle}, the connection is lower block \
triangular. The 12 by 12 rational block is the d=1 ordinary-vacuum mass \
connection. Since the original propagator masses x0^2,x2^2,x3^2 are \
independent of a, the logarithmic diagonal blocks vanish; their derivatives \
are the explicit rational source maps below. The homogeneous triangle block \
is exactly the earlier eleven-master epsilon=0 connection. Only the three \
triangle-to-lower-weight blocks remain as named lifted-IBP slots.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"rationalConnectionA", "=", 
        RowBox[{"RationalConnectionA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"logYToRationalA", "=", RowBox[{"LogYToRationalConnectionA", 
          "[", "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"logXToRationalA", "=", 
        RowBox[{"LogXToRationalConnectionA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"triangleHomogeneousA", "=", 
        RowBox[{"TriangleHomogeneousConnectionA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{TagBox["rationalConnectionA", Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], ",", TagBox["logYToRationalA", 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], ",", 
          TagBox["logXToRationalA", Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]], ",", TagBox["triangleHomogeneousA", 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]}], "}"}]}]], 
   "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"connectionTemplateA", "=", 
        RowBox[{"FiniteConnectionTemplateA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "connectionTemplateA", 
            "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"FiniteConnectionStrictUpperBlockCheckA", 
            "[", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"blockRanges", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Values", "[", RowBox[{"FiniteNestedBlockRangesA", "[", 
            "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", TagBox[RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
         RowBox[{RowBox[{"If", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", RowBox[{"connectionTemplateA", 
                       "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", RowBox[{RowBox[{"blockRanges", 
                          "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", "i", 
                          "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}], ",", RowBox[
                          {"blockRanges", "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", "j", 
                          "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}]}], 
                       "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "===", "0"}], 
               ",", "0", ",", RowBox[{"Symbol", "[", RowBox[{"\"A\"", "<>", 
                   RowBox[{"ToString", "[", "i", "]"}], "<>", RowBox[
                    {"ToString", "[", "j", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"i", ",", "4"}], "}"}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"j", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
       Function[BoxForm`e$, MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]}]], "Input"], 
  Cell["8. Basis transformations", "Section"], Cell["The rational block is \
already lower triangular: factorized bubbles precede the four sunrise \
masters. The logarithmic blocks lie below it and have zero diagonal. The only \
nontrivial leading-singularity transformation is therefore the \
eleven-dimensional triangle transformation derived earlier. For any \
transformation T(a), the helper evaluates (partial_a T) T^(-1)+T A T^(-1), \
including the necessary gauge term.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"triangularTemplateA", "=", 
        RowBox[{"FiniteTriangularConnectionTemplateA", "[", "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "triangularTemplateA", 
            "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"FiniteTriangularStrictUpperCheckA", "[", 
            "]"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"transformRule", "=", 
        TagBox[RowBox[{"triangularA", "=", RowBox[
            {"TransformFiniteConnectionA", "[", RowBox[{"fullA", ",", 
               "leadingSingularityTransform", ",", "aK"}], "]"}]}], 
         HoldForm]}], ";", "transformRule"}]], "Input"], 
  Cell["9. Verification summary", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"TestReport", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{"Length", "[", "rationalBasis", "]"}], ",", "12", 
              ",", RowBox[{"TestID", "\[Rule]", 
                "\"rational-sector-count\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
                "finiteNestedBasis", "]"}], ",", "31", ",", RowBox[{"TestID", 
                "\[Rule]", "\"finite-total-count\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"DuplicateFreeQ", 
                "[", "finiteNestedBasis", "]"}], ",", "True", ",", 
              RowBox[{"TestID", "\[Rule]", "\"basis-is-duplicate-free\""}]}], 
            "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", 
            RowBox[{"poleCancellation", ",", "0", ",", RowBox[{"TestID", 
                "\[Rule]", "\"bubble-pole-cancellation\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", 
                "rationalConnectionA", "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"12", ",", "12"}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"TestID", 
                "\[Rule]", "\"rational-connection-dimensions\""}]}], "]"}], 
          ",", RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", RowBox[
             {RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "logYToRationalA", "]"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"4", ",", "12"}], "}"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"TestID", "\[Rule]", "\"log-y-source-dimensions\""}]}], 
            "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "logXToRationalA", "]"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"4", ",", "12"}], "}"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"TestID", "\[Rule]", "\"log-x-source-dimensions\""}]}], 
            "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "triangleHomogeneousA", "]"}], 
              ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"11", ",", "11"}], "}"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"TestID", "\[Rule]", 
                "\"triangle-block-dimensions\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", RowBox[
             {RowBox[{"FiniteTriangularStrictUpperCheckA", "[", "]"}], ",", 
              "True", ",", RowBox[{"TestID", "\[Rule]", 
                "\"strict-upper-triangular-check\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"VerificationTest", "[", RowBox[
             {RowBox[{"FiniteConnectionStrictUpperBlockCheckA", "[", "]"}], 
              ",", "True", ",", RowBox[{"TestID", "\[Rule]", 
                "\"lower-block-filtration\""}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]], 
   "Input"], Cell["Scope note. The finite flat connection, the \
twelve-dimensional rational block, both logarithm-to-rational blocks, and the \
eleven-dimensional homogeneous triangle block are explicit. The remaining \
symbols ctr, cty and ctx are the triangle-to-rational, triangle-to-Ly and \
triangle-to-Lx source blocks. They require a lifted outer IBP reduction of \
the inhomogeneous terms in the triangle differential equation and are \
intentionally not presented as already-reduced coefficients.", "Text"]}, 
 WindowTitle -> "Cosmological Baikov: finite nested basis", 
 StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
